<div class="space-y-3">
    <p class="text-center font-semibold">DEALER AGREEMENT<br><span class="font-normal text-xs">(In duplicate / Original with the Organization and a copy with the Dealer)</span></p>
    <p>THE AGREEMENT made and entered into this <strong x-text="agreementDateText"></strong> by and between {{ $company }}, a company registered in India and having its office at ERA Galleria, 2nd Floor, Near JCD Vidyapeeth, Barnala Road, Sirsa, Haryana 125055 (hereinafter termed the Company), which expression shall unless repugnant to the context or contrary to the meaning thereof include its successors and assigns on the ONE PART, and <strong x-text="snapshot.business_name || '[dealer name]'"></strong> (hereinafter referred to as the DEALER, which term shall mean and include, wherever the context so permits, their heirs, assigns, successors and administrators) of the OTHER PART.</p>
    <p>WITNESSETH: WHEREAS the Company has agreed to appoint <strong x-text="snapshot.business_name || '[dealer name]'"></strong> as its Dealer on a non-exclusive basis and the Dealer has agreed to act as a Dealer of the Company at <strong x-text="snapshot.city || '[place]'"></strong>, taluk/tehsil <strong x-text="snapshot.tehsil || '[tehsil]'"></strong>, in the district of <strong x-text="snapshot.district || '[district]'"></strong> in the State of <strong x-text="snapshot.state || '[state]'"></strong>, subject to the terms and conditions mentioned hereinafter.</p>

    <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2">
        <li><strong>PERIOD.</strong> The appointment shall initially be on probation for a period of 12 months during which the material shall be supplied on cash and carry basis. The Dealer shall be regularized after the review of the performance appraisal of the dealer during the probation period.</li>
        <li><strong>PRODUCTS.</strong> The Company shall ordinarily offer for sale products manufactured, imported, procured and marketed by it from time to time.</li>
        <li><strong>PACKING.</strong> The size, quantity, weight or volume contained in each packing of Kisan Urea and other products and the packing material used shall be as deemed appropriate by the Company.</li>
        <li><strong>QUANTITY.</strong> The quantity of Kisan Urea and other products that the Company shall accept for supply to the Dealer against his oral/written indent shall be subject to the availability of the products and the Company's sales plan/programme. The Dealer shall have no claim against the Company for non-acceptance of the whole or any part of the quantities indented orally or in writing by the dealer for the supplies.</li>
        <li><strong>PRODUCT RELEASE.</strong> The dealer shall lift the monthly targeted quantities of the Company's products allotted to him. The Company's District Officer shall issue to the dealer a Delivery Order specifying the quantity of Kisan Urea and other products authorized for delivery to the dealer from the designated warehouse. The Dealer, accepting the release of Kisan Urea and other products by the Company, shall sign on all copies of the Delivery Order.</li>
        <li><strong>PRICES.</strong> The Company shall have the right to fix and convey the prices of its products, at which the dealer shall pay for the products purchased by the dealer. Price revision, taxes, duties and levies made applicable by the Central or State Govt. or other local bodies shall be payable by the dealer effective from the dates such revisions are made applicable, whether communicated to the dealer separately by the Company or not. The taxes, duties or levies are over and above the notified prices.</li>
        <li><strong>COMMISSION AND REBATES.</strong> The Company at its option shall fix, revise and notify from time to time the commission and rebates payable to the dealer on the sale of its products, if applicable.</li>
        <li><strong>DELIVERY.</strong>
            <ol class="list-[lower-alpha] pl-5">
                <li>The Company shall instruct its Handling &amp; Transport Agent at rake-point/warehouse for issue of the products to the dealer against production of a valid delivery order issued by the Company.</li>
                <li>The method and place of delivery shall be determined and communicated to the dealer by the Company from time to time.</li>
                <li>The title to and risk of loss of the products delivered to the dealer shall pass on to the dealer upon loading into the road transport vehicle and obtaining acknowledgement. Block Transfer: in case the product due for delivery to the dealer has been transferred to the Dealer account at the Company's field warehouse, delivery of the products against delivery order shall be arranged as soon as practicable.</li>
                <li>Charges for loading at the Company's field warehouse shall be borne by the Company.</li>
            </ol>
        </li>
        <li><strong>PAYMENT.</strong> 9.1 The dealer shall make necessary financial arrangement for the value of the products requested by him and accepted for release by the Company before issue of the delivery order in such manner acceptable to the Company. The supplies shall be made as per company sales terms. 9.2 Products delivered to the dealer will be invoiced at the prices prevailing or applicable on the date of issue of D.O. by the Company for such products.</li>
        <li><strong>SALES PROMOTION.</strong> The dealer shall promote the sale of Kisan Urea and other Company products as mutually decided from time to time and by distribution and exhibition of the printed literature, posters and dealer signboards supplied to the dealer by the Company.</li>
        <li><strong>TRADE MARKS.</strong> 11.1 The dealer shall use the Company's trade name and trade mark only to the extent required to identify, advertise and sell Kisan Urea &amp; other products. The dealer shall not mix, blend, dilute or contaminate any bag of Kisan Urea &amp; other products or use Kisan Urea and other products for any purpose not covered by this agreement. The Company shall have the right at all times to inspect the products in the possession of the dealer and also in the possession of the dealer's branches/sub-dealers, if any, to ensure that all conditions and statutory obligations are duly complied with and to determine adherence to quality and trade mark authorizations. 11.2 The Company may make any change in its trade mark and trade name which are used on and for products as it may consider necessary.</li>
        <li><strong>WARRANTY AND CLAIMS.</strong> 12.1 The dealer's claim for defective packaging/defective product/shortage of any product or for any other reason shall be made in writing to the Company's area office assigned to the area of the dealer within the prescribed time and in the manner stipulated by the Company from time to time. 12.2 The Company shall have the right and the dealer shall give the opportunity to make such inspection as it deems necessary to determine validity of such claim. 12.3 No claim by either party for indirect, consequential or remote damages shall be entertained.</li>
        <li><strong>GENERAL.</strong>
            <p class="mt-1">13.1 DEPOSIT. This appointment as dealer is subject to the dealer making a security deposit of the desired amount through RTGS/NEFT to the Company. For this the EMD amount deposited by the dealer along with the Dealer application shall be converted into a refundable Security Deposit on appointment as dealer. The Company shall, however, have the right to appropriate the deposit for any breach or failure on the part of the dealer without prejudice to other remedies available to it and, when so appropriated, the dealer shall replenish the amount appropriated. On termination of the Dealer, the deposit shall be refunded after adjustment of any final claim that the Company may have against the dealer, along with interest as per company policy. The Security Deposit will not carry any interest and will be refunded on termination / resignation of the Dealer and after the company's property is returned by the dealer.</p>
            <p class="mt-1">13.2 The Company has the right at any time and from time to time to appoint other Dealers or any other agency to sell and market Kisan Urea &amp; other products, besides selling and distributing directly, in the area(s) of the dealer's operational area.</p>
            <p class="mt-1">13.3 The dealer shall comply with the rules, regulations and procedures of the Essential Commodities Act, the Fertilizer (Control) Order 1985, the Fertilizer (Movement Control) Order 1973, the Legal Metrology Act 2009, the Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules 2011 and any other law or Govt. regulations, now existing or enforced at any future date, or any amendments made thereto from time to time. The dealer shall in particular comply with the provisions relating to licences, licence fee, storage facilities, records, submission of returns and reports, inspection by authorized officials, prices, quality of agricultural inputs and packages and other directives/laws/regulations that may be brought into force from time to time. The dealer must have GST registration as may be applicable in the state.</p>
            <p class="mt-1">13.4 (a) The dealer shall obtain a Certificate of Registration immediately after receiving the Source Certificate on Form 'O' issued by the Company. In case the Dealer is already a registered dealer of fertilizers, he will arrange to get the Company's name and products endorsed in the Fertilizer Registration Certificate (FRC). (b) In case there is any change in the constitution of the dealer's firm/agency as declared in the application form, in terms of change in partners/directors or in any other way, the dealer shall notify the Company in writing of such changes within one month from the date of such changes. The Company reserves the right to approve or disapprove the change(s) so made in the constitution of the firm/agency, as the case may be, at its sole discretion.</p>
            <p class="mt-1">13.5 The dealer shall maintain proper accounts for all Kisan Urea &amp; other products purchased and sold, as well as retail separately, and duly report to the Company and the Distt. Agriculture Deptt. as per procedure.</p>
            <p class="mt-1">13.6 Company representatives shall from time to time call on the dealer in order to keep the Company informed about the marketing conditions and evaluate the effectiveness of the Dealer's contribution to the overall marketing programmes.</p>
            <p class="mt-1">13.7 The Dealer shall receive acknowledgement of subsidized fertilizer stocks from its wholesalers, retailers and outlets in the iFMS (Integrated Fertilizer Management System) within the time period prescribed by the Department of Fertilizers (DoF) and the Company. The Dealer shall also ensure that the sale of subsidized fertilizers supplied by and/or on behalf of the Company, by its retailers, wholesalers or other authorized entities, is carried out strictly through the Point of Sale (POS) system. If any subsidized fertilizer quantities supplied to the dealer are not acknowledged by the dealer and/or not sold through the POS system by retailers or other authorized entities in iFMS, and the subsidy amount for said quantity is not released by DoF / FICC (Fertilizer Industry Coordination Committee), the Dealer shall be liable for recovery/debit of the full value of the material, including subsidy and other related expenditure/charges (if applicable).</p>
        </li>
        <li><strong>TERMINATION.</strong> Without prejudice to the claim of any dues to either party, this appointment shall be terminated by either party on 30 days' notice in writing sent by Registered Post. Notwithstanding this provision, the Company shall be entitled to terminate the Dealer without notice if any of the conditions contained herein are contravened by the Dealer, or if any of the information furnished in the Dealer application is found to be not true, or if the Dealer is suspected of indulging in trade practices detrimental to the interest of the Company.</li>
        <li><strong>ARBITRATION.</strong> Any dispute or difference whatsoever arising between the parties out of or relating to the construction, meaning, scope, operation or effect of this contract or the validity or the breach thereof shall be resolved amicably through negotiations by the parties. A "Notice of Dispute" shall be given by the party seeking resolution of a dispute to the other party. If the dispute is not resolved within thirty (30) days from the notice, the dispute shall be referred to arbitration as follows. A written notice shall be given by the Dealer invoking arbitration to the Company through its Director (Marketing). Where the claim, including determination of interest if any, up to the date of commencement of arbitration does not exceed Rs. five crore, the reference shall be made to a sole arbitrator mutually agreed by the parties; in case of disagreement, the sole arbitrator shall be appointed in accordance with the Arbitration &amp; Conciliation Act, 1996. Where the claim exceeds Rs. five crore, the reference shall be made to an arbitral tribunal of three arbitrators: each party shall nominate one arbitrator within 30 days from the date of receipt of the notice invoking arbitration and the two nominated arbitrators shall appoint the presiding arbitrator within 30 days thereafter; if a party fails to nominate, or the two arbitrators fail to appoint the presiding arbitrator, the appointment shall be made in accordance with the Arbitration &amp; Conciliation Act, 1996. The arbitration proceedings shall be governed by the Arbitration &amp; Conciliation Act, 1996 and any statutory modification or re-enactment thereof and the rules made thereunder. The seat and venue of arbitration shall be at Panchkula Chandigarh (place of Zonal Office). The cost of the proceedings shall be borne equally by the parties unless otherwise directed by the arbitral tribunal. The decision of the arbitral tribunal shall be final and binding on all parties.</li>
        <li><strong>JURISDICTION.</strong> This Agreement shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of Courts at Panchkula Chandigarh (place of Zonal Office).</li>
    </ol>
    <p>IN WITNESS WHEREOF the parties have set their hands on the day, month and year mentioned above, in the presence of the witnesses named below.</p>
</div>
